<template>
  <j-page class="store-page detail-page">
    <main>
      <nav class="breadcrumb-line" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/" data-jv-router>Catalog</a><span>/</span><span>Databases</span><span>/</span><strong>MySQL</strong>
      </nav>

      <section class="detail-hero" aria-labelledby="mysql-title">
        <span class="package-icon package-icon--mysql package-icon--large" aria-hidden="true">MY</span>
        <div class="detail-hero__copy">
          <div class="package-badges">
            <j-badge class="trust-badge">Official</j-badge>
            <j-badge class="preview-badge">Source kit</j-badge>
          </div>
          <span class="package-publisher">Nextera / mysql</span>
          <h1 id="mysql-title">MySQL</h1>
          <p>Stateful MySQL 8.4 with fenced storage, secret delivery, health checks, resource limits, and an operator-tested restore path.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <j-alert class="readiness-alert">
        <j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</j-icon>
        <div>
          <strong>This is a reviewed source kit, not a registry release.</strong>
          <p>The immutable package digest, publisher signature, SBOM, and install evidence will appear here after the publishing pipeline is live.</p>
        </div>
      </j-alert>

      <div class="detail-layout">
        <section class="detail-content" aria-labelledby="overview-title">
          <j-card class="detail-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Operational design</span>
              <h2 id="overview-title">What this kit protects</h2>
              <p>The database files live on a NexRun volume with an exclusive fenced lease, not in the container's writable layer. Restart, redeploy, and daemon recovery preserve the data while the fencing epoch prevents a stale second writer.</p>
              <ul class="feature-list">
                <li><j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</j-icon><span>MySQL 8.4 OCI runtime</span></li>
                <li><j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</j-icon><span>Required root password delivered as a scoped secret file</span></li>
                <li><j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</j-icon><span>Readiness through <code>mysqladmin ping</code></span></li>
                <li><j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</j-icon><span>Graceful 60-second termination period</span></li>
                <li><j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</j-icon><span>Snapshot, logical, and point-in-time recovery guidance</span></li>
              </ul>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>

          <j-card class="detail-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Current source-kit flow</span>
              <h2>Review before deployment</h2>
              <j-list class="install-list">
                <j-list-item><j-item-section class="step-number">1</j-item-section><j-item-section><j-item-label>Install and inspect NexRun</j-item-label><j-item-label>Run <code>nexrun doctor</code> on the target Linux runtime.</j-item-label></j-item-section></j-list-item>
                <j-list-item><j-item-section class="step-number">2</j-item-section><j-item-section><j-item-label>Prepare storage and configuration</j-item-label><j-item-label>Create the data and configuration volumes, then place <code>my.cnf</code> on the read-only configuration volume.</j-item-label></j-item-section></j-list-item>
                <j-list-item><j-item-section class="step-number">3</j-item-section><j-item-section><j-item-label>Create the scoped secret</j-item-label><j-item-label>Use NexRun secret tooling to create <code>mysql-root-password</code>; never place it in the manifest.</j-item-label></j-item-section></j-list-item>
                <j-list-item><j-item-section class="step-number">4</j-item-section><j-item-section><j-item-label>Validate and deploy</j-item-label><j-item-label>Validate the IDEL workload locally before changing runtime state.</j-item-label></j-item-section></j-list-item>
                <j-list-item><j-item-section class="step-number">5</j-item-section><j-item-section><j-item-label>Complete a restore drill</j-item-label><j-item-label>Retain measured RPO/RTO and restore evidence before production use.</j-item-label></j-item-section></j-list-item>
              </j-list>
              <pre class="command-block"><code>git clone https://github.com/nextera-one/nexrun.git
cd nexrun
nexrun doctor
nexrun validate -f examples/mysql/mysql.idel.yaml
nexrun deploy -f examples/mysql/mysql.idel.yaml</code></pre>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
        </section>

        <aside class="requirement-column" aria-label="Package requirements">
          <j-card class="requirement-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Runtime profile</span>
              <dl class="requirement-list">
                <div><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>OCI / containerd</dd></div>
                <div><dt>CPU</dt><dd>2,000 millicores</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Memory</dt><dd>2 GiB</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Processes</dt><dd>512</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Port</dt><dd>TCP 3306</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Architectures</dt><dd>AMD64, ARM64</dd></div>
              </dl>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
          <j-card class="requirement-card">
            <j-card-section>
              <span class="eyebrow">Instance configuration</span>
              <h2>2 volumes</h2>
              <p><code>mysql-data</code><br /><code>mysql-conf</code></p>
              <j-separator></j-separator>
              <h2>1 required secret</h2>
              <p><code>mysql-root-password</code></p>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
          <j-card class="requirement-card requirement-card--warning">
            <j-card-section>
              <j-icon class="glyph-icon" aria-hidden="true">!</j-icon>
              <h2>Production note</h2>
              <p>Single-node MySQL is not database HA. Host loss causes downtime until the fenced volume is recovered or restored.</p>
            </j-card-section>
          </j-card>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </main>
  </j-page>
</template>
